      'Too small a cuff squashes the urethra: retention and tissue damage. Too large a cuff does not close properly: leakage. Neither problem is fixed by choosing a higher-pressure balloon. Check how the cuff finally sits and how the device works, with a leak test when that is appropriate. If what you see and what you measured disagree, find out why.',
