      'After a straightforward implant, take the catheter out early and check that he voids. If he cannot, assess the device state, swelling, the cuff fit and any obstruction, drain the bladder safely, and do not make repeated blind catheter attempts. Day-case pathways are feasible for selected men: the BAUS 2026 audit sent 88 per cent home the same day, and the 2026 meta-analysis found no significant excess of retention or emergency visits, with wide uncertainty. That supports a selected pathway with proven emptying, not a rule for everyone.',
