      'The answer may be retraining, bladder treatment, replacing a component, a new cuff strategy, or removal. In an old system, discuss replacing the whole thing. The French national cohort reminds us that second implants have 68 per cent reintervention-free survival at five years, and that only one in five men whose first device was removed ever received another. Repeated failure or a damaged urethra needs a specialist opinion before another operation that uses up tissue.',
